# Minecraft Version(s): 26.3
## Merl shows you the way
- **[Guide me]** now has Merl herself walk ahead of you along the way, holding a map. She waits when you fall behind and looks at you when you arrive. A few sparkles between you and her show the way around corners. Only you see her
- New option `guideMerl` (default `true`): turn it off for just the sparkle trail

## Sparkle trail fixes
- The trail finds its way out of buildings: it goes through doors, fence gates and trapdoors and over carpet, instead of leading you into the wall facing your destination
- It always heads for your actual destination, so it no longer gets stuck aiming at a spot inside a hill or another building
- When the way out is long (out of a big base or a cave), it looks much further before giving up, and it never shows a trail that just ends at a wall
- The sparkles are easier to see again
- On the ground it never draws a line through walls anymore; when there really is no way from where you stand, the action bar shows a short "(no path)"
- The direction on the action bar no longer flickers between two (like "north" and "northwest") as you walk

## Trail debug
- `/nicemerl guide debug` shows on the action bar what the path search did (steps, whether it got through, how far it looked), to help find spots where the trail gets stuck

## Turn the trail off by asking
- *"Stop the route"*, *"turn off GPS"*, *"don't guide me"*, *"cancel navigation"* or *"no more sparkles"* turn the trail off, just like `/nicemerl guide stop`

## Smaller changes
- Merl mannequins look at the closest player within a few blocks, and say their message when you left- or right-click them or look them in the eyes from up close (once a minute; new option `mannequinGreetOnLook`)
- Merl's "Merl:" prefix is no longer bold
